                <pb facs="0455" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/14326: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-02T18:00:00-04:00">September 2, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. For your information, the following is the text of a message from the
                    President to the Shah dated September 2, 1941 in response to a message which the
                    President received from His Majesty. It should also be considered as a response
                    to the message of the Iranian Government transmitted by your 106, August 25, 6
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
